  {
    "id": "857359b8a18a1a44a896",
    "source": "One roll per uncertain action; do not chain repeated rolls for the same attempt. Trivial actions (walking, talking, buying a drink) need no roll, but no roll does not mean no bookkeeping: call open_shop before describing a place's wares, never pricing them in prose; every purchase, sale, or trade goes through ONE purchase call (at a shop in SHOPS HERE the shop trades from its shelf at its own prices, which haggle moves; anywhere else the server prices anything the book lists: list price to buy, half to sell, full value for gems, art, and trade goods; your price counts only for something nothing prices. It moves the gold and the item together and refuses what the purse cannot cover; an unaffordable price is a fact of the scene). Gifts, loot, and theft still use grant_item/remove_item with modify_gold only when coins alone move; anything set down, dropped, knocked away or handed to an ally goes through handle_item (it lies where it fell, never destroyed), and so does a shield put on or off or a weapon drawn or stowed. Never narrate money or items changing hands without the tool call.",
    "sourceHash": "857359b8a18a1a44a89620b6393269a737bcf9c74be56f77f095093efb6c2fc4",
    "kinds": [
      "display-property"
    ],
    "sites": [
      {
        "file": "src/lib/dm/prompt-rules.ts",
        "line": 142
      }
    ]
  },
